From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] tu: no reserved descriptor set for VKD3D-Proton

VKD3D-Proton's root signatures need 5 descriptor sets. The A6xx GPUs have 5, and Turnip keeps one
for dynamic buffer descriptors (UNIFORM_BUFFER_DYNAMIC, STORAGE_BUFFER_DYNAMIC), leaving 4: Direct3D
12 games hung before their first frame (Stray, UTDeck stage 3.2b), and the environment variable
tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set=true fixed it. As a default for every program that variable would
also reach zink in the same process, which uses dynamic uniform buffers, while Turnip still
reports them as supported. VKD3D-Proton never uses dynamic buffer descriptors (neither does
DXVK), so turn the option on for the vkd3d engine only, next to Turnip's other vkd3d default.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf b/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
index 0596f6c..6d13509 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
@@ -41,6 +41,13 @@
         </engine>
 	<engine engine_name_match="vkd3d">
 	    <option name="tu_enable_softfloat32" value="true" />
+	    <!--
+	        VKD3D-Proton's root signatures need 5 descriptor sets, and A6xx has 5, of which
+	        Turnip keeps one for dynamic buffer descriptors, which VKD3D-Proton never uses:
+	        without the 5th, Direct3D 12 games hang before their first frame (Stray). Only
+	        for vkd3d: zink and other Vulkan programs use dynamic buffers.
+	    -->
+	    <option name="tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set" value="true" />
 	</engine>
         <engine engine_name_match="ANGLE">
             <!--
